==============================================================================
PART 4.  Cross-checks and negative controls
==============================================================================
  trivial cycle as a fake period-p cycle gives R_r = 4^p - 3^p at every
  rotation, p in {1,2,3,4,7,11}: agrees with cycles.md 12.6.1.
  published p=7 instance n=94: gamma = 6.744 (12.8.3: 6.74),
  all seven rotations pass, divisibility fails -- reproduced by this
  file's independent transport-recurrence evaluator.
  negative control: the FLAT depth profile at p=12, n=251 fails q <= R_r (min R_r / q = 0.0000) -- the
  geometric shape is doing real work, the test is not vacuous.
  negative control: p=10, n=106 has gamma = 1.006 (delta near 1) and fails q <= R_r, as the two-sided reading of
  Part 1 predicts: too SMALL a gamma is as fatal as too large.
  negative control: p=14, n=465 has gamma = 1.008 (delta near 1) and fails q <= R_r, as the two-sided reading of
  Part 1 predicts: too SMALL a gamma is as fatal as too large.

